            "review_title": "Review at Sho Bu",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nMassive portions at this Japanese fine-dining restaurant that's Korean-owned.\nJun 2023 • Family\nThis quiet and unpretentious restaurant has been a longstanding icon along this road with a high turnover of shops - probably been around for 10 years or more.\n\nYou can get the regular lunch sets at 300+vnd per person, or if you're really hungry and craving for sashimi, go for their Shobu Business Course (990,000vnd++) or Shobu Tuna Course (1,350,000vnd++) per course. We ordered one of each and there was so much food - every portion was so massive and satisfying - that we had to pack the cooked portions such as soups, Korean pancakes and tempura for dinner. The Korean chef was around to explain to us what each sashimi was, and what side dishes they go well with.\n\nDEFINITELY reserve in advance, because they need to prep the sashimi in advance.\nRead more\nWritten December 22, 2023",
